# ============================================================
# vertex — .vercelignore
# Added as part of the Sept 2026 exposed-key remediation.
#
# Vercel is only meant to serve the static front-end (html/css/js/data).
# Everything below belongs to the separate Cloudflare Worker deployment
# (`wrangler deploy`) and has no business being uploaded to Vercel, let
# alone being reachable as a public static file at
# https://<your-app>.vercel.app/worker.js
#
# None of these currently contain live secrets (secrets live in
# Cloudflare env vars / `wrangler secret put`), but keeping backend
# source and infra config out of the CDN-served bundle is basic
# defense-in-depth: it stops anyone from reading your worker's internal
# logic, KV key naming scheme, model routing, rate-limit thresholds, etc.
# ============================================================

# Cloudflare Worker source + config — deployed via wrangler, not Vercel
worker.js
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml

# Local Cloudflare dev/secrets files (should never exist in git anyway,
# but belt-and-suspenders in case one is ever created locally)
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.wrangler/

# One-off key-generation utility — dev tool only, not part of the app
vapid-generator.html

# Tooling / repo metadata that doesn't need to be on the CDN
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
README.md

# VECTOR: BLACKLINE multiplayer service (a separate Cloudflare Worker) and the
# source-code backup. Deployed by Cloudflare from GitHub, not served by Vercel.
vector/server/
vector/tests/
vector-source/
